---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildFAQSchema } from "../../lib/seo";

const pageFaqs = [
  {
    question: "What is CELPIP Speaking Task 7 testing?",
    answer:
      "Task 7 is testing whether you can express an opinion clearly, support it with reasons, and keep speaking in an organized way.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do I need to discuss both sides in Task 7?",
    answer:
      "No. You can mention another view briefly, but the main job is to explain your own opinion well.",
  },
  {
    question: "What usually lowers Task 7 scores?",
    answer:
      "Scores often drop when the opinion is unclear, the support is repetitive, or the answer is too short to develop the idea properly.",
  },
];

const pageStructuredData = [
  buildBreadcrumbSchema(Astro.site, [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Blog", path: "/blog/" },
    { name: "CELPIP Speaking Task 7 Opinion Strategy", path: "/blog/celpip-speaking-task-7-opinion-strategy/" },
  ]),
  buildFAQSchema(pageFaqs),
];
---

<Layout
  title="CELPIP Speaking Task 7 | Express Opinions Clearly"
  description="A CELPIP Speaking Task 7 guide with a simple opinion structure, clearer support, and better ways to sound organized under pressure."
  type="article"
  keywords="CELPIP speaking task 7, CELPIP opinion strategy, CELPIP speaking opinions"
  structuredData={pageStructuredData}
>
  <article class="section guide-article">
    <a class="guide-back-link" href="/blog">Back to blog</a>

    <header class="guide-header">
      <span class="guide-tag">CELPIP speaking guide</span>
      <h1 style="margin: 0;">CELPIP Speaking Task 7</h1>
      <div class="guide-meta">
        <span>March 17, 2026</span>
        <span>6 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="guide-lead">
      <p>
        CELPIP Speaking Task 7 rewards clear thinking more than dramatic language. The
        strongest answers tell the listener exactly what you think, then support that opinion
        with reasons that are easy to follow.
      </p>
      <p>
        A simple, organized answer usually sounds much stronger than an ambitious answer that
        repeats itself or loses direction.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="guide-card">
      <h2>A simple Task 7 structure</h2>
      <div class="guide-steps">
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>State your opinion</h3>
            <p>Give your answer clearly in the opening sentence.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Give your first reason</h3>
            <p>Choose a reason that is easy to explain under time pressure.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Add support</h3>
            <p>Use an example, result, or short comparison to make the reason stronger.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">4</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Close clearly</h3>
            <p>End with one sentence that reinforces your position.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>Example frame</h2>
      <div class="guide-example">
        <p><strong>Opinion:</strong> Personally, I believe this is the better choice.</p>
        <p><strong>Reason:</strong> The main reason is that it would save time and reduce stress.</p>
        <p><strong>Support:</strong> For example, people with busy schedules usually need the most practical option.</p>
        <p><strong>Closing:</strong> That is why I would definitely support this choice.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>What often sounds weak</h2>
      <table class="guide-mistake-table">
        <tr>
          <th>Weak move</th>
          <th>Better move</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The opinion appears too late.</td>
          <td>State it immediately.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The same reason is repeated in different words.</td>
          <td>Add one useful example instead.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The support is too vague.</td>
          <td>Use a specific result, situation, or comparison.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The answer sounds memorized.</td>
          <td>Keep a frame, but use natural wording.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>Next step</h2>
      <div class="guide-links">
        <a href="/blog/celpip-speaking-task-5-comparing-options">
          <strong>Read the Task 5 guide</strong>
          <span>Compare clear opinion speaking with comparison and persuasion tasks.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/blog/celpip-speaking-part2">
          <strong>Read the Task 2 guide</strong>
          <span>See how personal storytelling differs from opinion speaking.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/celpip/speaking">
          <strong>Go to the CELPIP speaking hub</strong>
          <span>Open more speaking guides and related lesson links.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <div class="guide-faq">
        {pageFaqs.map((item) => (
          <details class="card">
            <summary>{item.question}</summary>
            <p class="muted" style="margin-top: var(--s-2); margin-bottom: 0;">{item.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
